\ ==== reload literals ====

\ reload (forget_user) must preserve string-literal objects baked into the
\ compiled-in vocabulary. `run` is `: run " +" split start-process ;` — its
\ " +" regex is an init-time arena object. forget_user used to free every
\ object (n_objects=0), dangling that literal, so run/ls broke after a reload.
\ Now objects below the init watermark survive. Non-empty output (1) proves it.
reload
"echo marker" run read-out size 0 > . cr

clear

\ ==== load library ====

\ load-library ( name -- ) — load lib/<name>[.telic] from beside the telic
\ binary, symlinks resolved, independent of the process cwd.

\ === a bare name gains .telic; the plot library defines figure ===
"plot" load-library
' figure drop "loaded" . cr                  \ loaded

\ === an explicit extension is used as given ===
"plot.telic" load-library
"again" . cr                                 \ again

\ === a missing library errors (message elided: it carries a machine path) ===
[: "no-such-library" load-library :] catch nip . cr   \ 1

clear
